    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `selfLink` field to the owner representation, returning `/api/owners/` followed by the owner's id.\n\nFollowing the existing conventions in this codebase (DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec, and derived fields are either backed by an Owner getter or computed via a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression \u2014 as `displayName` and `initials` already are), I made two small edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a readOnly `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (right after `initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")` to `toOwnerDto`, matching the pattern used for the other computed fields.\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `\"selfLink\": \"/api/owners/{id}\"`. The test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
